Database migrations (Alembic)

- Dev/test (SQLite, the default): no action needed - tables are still
  auto-created on first use for a zero-setup experience.
- Production (Postgres): schema is managed here, not by create_all(). Run:
    alembic upgrade head
  after deploying any release that changed src/db/models.py.
- Adopting Alembic on a database that already has tables from before this
  existed (i.e. created by the old create_all()-only path): stamp it at the
  baseline revision first, then upgrade normally:
    alembic stamp fa0f491b5cac   # matches the schema at Stage 1/2
    alembic upgrade head
- After changing src/db/models.py, generate a new migration with:
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
  then read the generated file before committing it - autogenerate is a
  good first draft, not a guarantee (it won't catch every kind of change,
  e.g. renamed columns look like a drop+add unless you edit it by hand).
